      "math_academy_id": "q-129210",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows of  $A$ are $1$ and $3$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+3=4.$",
